Most religions on Basis have a designated one holy day during the week. In [[Sunneism]] and [[Mōnaïsm]], it is on the day of [[Mōna]], while in [[Scildism]] and [[Ānism]], it is on the day of [[Basis]]. In [[Manigism]], they do not have a weekly holy day, but rather celebrate the [[Last Day of the Year]] as their holy day, representing a new cycle. 

